{
  "$comment": "Image placeholders on text-only routes. A route that can only send text writes one placeholder line per attached image, byte-identical on every end, and its outgoing request body carries no image block. On routes gated by the model's vision verdict, the placeholder is written only when the model's vision_input projects to outbound=placeholder: each byModel row is (model, verdict) -> expected outbound, asserted from the production outbound path. Rows without byModel (llama.cpp native, Gemini Interactions) are routes that send text only. Each end runs one test per case, named IMAGE_PLACEHOLDER_<id> (Web: it('IMAGE-PLACEHOLDER-<id> ...')), and asserts both the route declaration and the body produced by its production request builder for that route.",
  "v": 1,
  "cases": [
